===National Historic Sites===
* Included in the National Historic Site "Mount Fuji"

===Prefectural Natural Monuments===
* Fuji Sengen Shrine's Great Cedar - Located to the left of the Haiden, called "Fuji Taro Sugi," estimated to be around 1,000 years old.

===Prefectural Intangible Folk Cultural Properties===
* Kitaguchi Hongū Fuji Sengen Shrine Grand Kagura

===Municipal Tangible Cultural Properties===
* Kitaguchi Hongū Fuji Sengen Shrine main hall Ema (5 pieces) (附: Silk colored Fuji Mountain Northern View) (Paintings)
** Colored wooden panel painting of camellia and bamboo shoots (2 pieces) - Donated in Genwa 4 (1618) by Tosa-no-Kami Torii.
** Colored wooden panel painting of horse decoration and pine monkey (2 pieces) - Painted by Kano Tsuneshige, donated in Genroku 1 (1688) by Tajima-no-Kami Akimoto.
** Colored gold ground painting of divine horse (1 piece) - Painted by Kano Dokuen Nashin, donated in Genroku 11 (1698) by Noto-no-Kami Toda Tadashige.
* Wooden seated statues of guardian deities (附: pedestals) (Sculpture) - Two statues with blue and red garments, made in Eisho 17 (1520) by Minbu Hokkyo, a disciple of Hitachiobo from Gojō Ōmiya, Kyoto.
* Fuji Diary (Ancient document) - A travel diary written by Kamo Tadayoshi, a scholar of kokugaku residing in Edo, when he visited the area in Kansei 2 (1790).

===Municipal Natural Monuments===
* Kitaguchi Hongū Fuji Sengen Shrine's Cedar - Located behind the Haiden to the east, called "Fuji Jiro Sugi" and cherished by locals.
* Kitaguchi Hongū Fuji Sengen Shrine's Hinoki - Two hinoki trees fused at the base, called "Fuji Meoto Hinoki," meaning "Fuji Husband and Wife Cypress."

==Episode==
* According to the Deputy Priest, there was a business named Fujisan Jidōsha (Mount Fuji Automobile) operating on adjacent land. When the company went out of business, the land was nearly purchased by Chinese investors. Fuji Kyūkō stepped in and bought the land, offering it as a free parking lot for shrine visitors. According to the Deputy Priest, Fuji Kyūkō purchased the land "for the sake of the shrine out of goodwill" without any other intended use<ref>{{Citation|title=【前田日明】日本武尊の聖域を参拝！！不思議な現象も？【久保サラ夫妻】|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GaEeHx62UX4|accessdate=2021-06-15|language=ja-JP}}（7:40~)</ref>.

